                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_288">Knaresborough,
                        Yorkshire. Trinitarian convent</orgName><p>A scribal signature at the end:
                        'Explicit liber de Paternoster per Iohannem Kylyngwyke'. John of Kilnwick
                        was minister of the house of Trinitarian friars in Knaresborough, probably
                        c. 1380--1400, but the only explicit reference i from 1388, and he was still
                        alive as the legatee of a local (Healaugh) will in 1402. (Ex inform. Ralph
